---
import HubPage from '../components/HubPage.astro';
---
<HubPage hubId="tax-india">
  <section aria-labelledby="hub-guide" class="mt-12 max-w-3xl">
    <h2 id="hub-guide" class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-4">How to choose a tax calculator</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Begin with the <a href="/in/income-tax-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">income tax calculator</a> to compare the old and new regimes on your actual income and deductions. If you are salaried, the <a href="/in/salary-ctc-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">salary CTC calculator</a> shows what reaches your bank account each month after EPF and tax, and the <a href="/in/hra-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">HRA calculator</a> shows how much rent allowance is exempt, which only matters if you stay in the old regime.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">If you sell shares, mutual funds or property, use the <a href="/in/capital-gains-tax-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">capital gains tax calculator</a>, since short-term and long-term gains are taxed differently. When your tax for the year after TDS is ₹10,000 or more, the <a href="/in/advance-tax-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">advance tax calculator</a> splits it across the four instalment dates. The <a href="/in/tds-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">TDS calculator</a> shows the tax deducted at source on payments such as rent, commission or professional fees, and the <a href="/in/gst-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">GST calculator</a> adds or removes GST from a price at any slab.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">To check a supplier’s bill, use the <a href="/in/gst-calculator" class="text-accent font-medium hover:underline">GST calculator for inclusive prices and CGST/SGST/IGST splits</a>. Confirm the invoice rate and place of supply before applying the calculation.</p>
  </section>
</HubPage>
